#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(517.78pt, 790.056pt, "1 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(76.224pt, 81.96pt, "LED-based multibeam photoacoustics combined with electrical circuit-based modeling ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 97.82pt, "for the analysis of multispecies mass transport through thin membranes")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 121.46pt, "Pawel Rochowski ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 145.34pt, "Institute of Experimental Physics, Faculty of Mathematics, Physics and Informatics, University ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 166.1pt, "of Gdańsk, Wita Stwosza 57, 80-308 Gdańsk, Poland ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 194.78pt, "Correspondence: pawel.rochowski@ug.edu.pl ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 223.58pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 247.34pt, "This work develops photoacoustic-based experimental methods for comprehensive ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 263.18pt, "characterization of multispecies mass transport from donor compartments to thin-membrane ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 279.17pt, "acceptor systems in perfect contact, supported by dedicated mass transfer modeling framework. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 295.01pt, "Multibeam configurations are implemented in photoacoustic setups operating in front-side ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 310.85pt, "detection and diffuse-reflection geometries. The setups are calibrated and adjusted prior to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 326.69pt, "measurements by means of transmission-mode photoacoustic experiments conducted under ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 342.65pt, "steady-state conditions. Finally, the methodologies were applied to a model system undergoing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 358.49pt, "photoinduced decay, enabling characterization of bulk transport kinetics as well as interfacial ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 374.33pt, "equilibration monitored through time-dependent changes in interfacial reflectivity. For the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 390.17pt, "analysis of bulk transport data, a lumped electrical-circuit (EC) model is introduced. The model ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 406.13pt, "is formulated in tableau form, linking species population dynamics to an interaction matrix ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 421.97pt, "representing mass-transport couplings consistent with the underlying diffusion–reaction ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 437.81pt, "framework. A simplified approximation of the model is further proposed and validated against ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 453.65pt, "experimental results. The combined experimental–modeling framework provides an effective ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 469.63pt, "approach for quantitative analysis of coupled diffusion, reaction, and interfacial processes in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 485.35pt, "thin-membrane systems. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 509.35pt, "Keywords: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(136.34pt, 509.35pt, "photoacoustics; membrane transport; electrical circuit model; multibeam ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 525.07pt, "techniques; diffusion-reaction model.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.824pt, 549.19pt, "1.")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 549.19pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 572.95pt, "Studies of transport processes, including mass transport, are central to numerous scientific ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 588.79pt, "disciplines, ranging from biology and pharmaceutics to physics and Earth sciences, in both ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 604.63pt, "fundamental and applied research [1–4]. A key driver of progress in this area is the common ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 620.47pt, "structure of the governing physical laws, which are rooted in the thermodynamic relationship ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 636.43pt, "between fluxes and their conjugate driving forces [5]. This general framework underlies the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 652.3pt, "transport of energy, mass, and charge and facilitates a continuous exchange of concepts between ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 668.14pt, "disciplines that may otherwise appear only weakly connected at the theoretical and practical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 683.86pt, "levels. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 707.86pt, "The investigation of mass transport processes inherently relies on appropriate experimental ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 723.82pt, "techniques that enable the testing of proposed hypotheses. In applied research, well-established ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 739.66pt, "and widely accessible experimental methods, combined with robust data analysis approaches, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 755.496pt, "play a dominant role. A representative example is provided by techniques used in ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(517.78pt, 790.056pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81.72pt, "pharmaceutical sciences, such as Franz diffusion cells, which allow the determination of mass ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 97.7pt, "transport kinetics across a membrane within the framework of an assumed transport model (i.e. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 113.54pt, "diffusion-controlled transport in the absence of external driving stimuli) [6]. Conceptually ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 129.26pt, "similar approaches are employed in column experiments commonly used in Earth sciences [7]. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 153.26pt, "From the perspective of quantitative analysis, it is important to determine not only the amount ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 169.1pt, "of substance transported into the medium but also its chemical stability and the impact of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 185.06pt, "possible transformations on the overall transport process. Such capabilities can be provided by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 200.9pt, "spectroscopic detection methods, provided that the investigated species exhibit distinguishable ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 216.74pt, "spectral signatures. Another critical aspect is the ability to monitor processes ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(438.07pt, 216.74pt, "in situ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.5pt, 216.74pt, ", rather than ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 232.58pt, "inferring chemical degradation or transformation solely from their indirect effects on release ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 248.42pt, "kinetics measured downstream of the membrane. This requirement is addressed by several ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 264.38pt, "experimental approaches with varying spatial and temporal resolution, including tape stripping ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 280.25pt, "combined with appropriate detection techniques (spectroscopic or radiolabeling), photothermal ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 296.09pt, "methods, and, more recently, infrared microspectroscopy combined with Bayesian inference ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 311.81pt, "[8–11]. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 335.81pt, "Among the aforementioned approaches, photothermal methods, including photoacoustics, have ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 351.77pt, "emerged as powerful tools for non-destructive investigations with high spatial resolution. Their ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 367.61pt, "capability arises from the intrinsic mechanism of signal generation, which depends ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 383.45pt, "simultaneously on the optical absorption, thermal properties, and structural characteristics of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.29pt, "the sample [12,13]. By probing the propagation of thermal waves generated through modulated ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 415.25pt, "light absorption, depth-resolved profiling becomes feasible [14,15]. This enables high-precision ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 431.09pt, "quantification of mass uptake and, through appropriate modulation schemes, allows monitoring ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 446.81pt, "of transport processes as a function of sample depth. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 470.83pt, "Photoacoustic techniques have long been applied to studies of substance release and mass ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 486.67pt, "transport. To date, investigations have been performed in various configurations, employing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 502.51pt, "either modulated continuous-wave excitation or pulsed illumination across spectral ranges ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 518.47pt, "extending from the ultraviolet to the infrared. These approaches have consistently provided ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 534.31pt, "valuable datasets characterizing transport phenomena. Depending on the assumed transport ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 550.15pt, "model, the extracted parameters have included mass diffusion coefficients, thermal relaxation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 565.99pt, "times, and, indirectly, chemical reaction rate constants, binding kinetics, or advective transport ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 581.95pt, "contributions [16–19]. The indirect nature of some of these determinations arises from an ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 597.79pt, "inherent methodological limitation, namely the monitoring of a single spectral channel during ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 613.63pt, "the experiment. This constraint can complicate data interpretation and introduce dependence on ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 629.35pt, "the specific transport scenario assumed in the mathematical model. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 653.38pt, "A possible route to overcome this limitation is provided by multibeam photoacoustics. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 669.22pt, "According to Duhamel’s theorem, the thermal response of a sample to multiple excitations is ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 685.18pt, "expected to be linear and additive. Furthermore, the Rosencwaig–Gersho model predicts a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 701.02pt, "linear relationship between the thermally induced piston motion and the acoustic signal detected ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 716.86pt, "by the sensor. These premises led to the development of the multibeam photoacoustic (MBPA) ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 732.7pt, "modality, in which two or more beams simultaneously probe distinct spectral bands, for ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 748.656pt, "example corresponding to different absorbing species within a single sample. The method has ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 764.496pt, "been experimentally tested using linear configurations based on low-power, spatially divergent ")
]

