#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 397pt), 70.5pt, 614pt))[
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(517.78pt, 790.056pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81.72pt, "light sources (e.g., LEDs) and a non-resonant photoacoustic cell [20]. The measurements ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 97.7pt, "confirmed that the acoustic responses associated with individual excitation beams remain ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 113.54pt, "independent, provided that the separation between their modulation frequencies (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(468.1pt, 113.54pt, "Δf")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(478.54pt, 113.54pt, ") exceeds ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 129.38pt, "both the instrumental frequency instability and the effective detection bandwidth determined ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 145.1pt, "by the lock-in time constant and filter characteristics. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 169.1pt, "These considerations define the objectives of the present work. First, we introduce multibeam ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 185.06pt, "photoacoustics for the investigation of complex mass transport in systems containing pigments ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 200.9pt, "with distinct spectral properties, enabling direct characterization of multispecies transport ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 216.74pt, "without the need for additional ad hoc assumptions within the mathematical framework. In ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 232.58pt, "addition, a diffuse-reflectance photoacoustic configuration is implemented for the first time to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 248.42pt, "monitor interfacial properties during the permeation process, providing sensitive indicators of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 264.38pt, "interphase processes occurring at the donor–acceptor and acceptor–air boundaries. Second, the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 280.25pt, "previously developed electrical circuit-based (EC) model of mass transport is extended to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 296.09pt, "incorporate chemical degradation processes, leading to a more general diffusion–reaction EC ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 311.81pt, "model. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 335.81pt, "To validate the proposed methodology and model, an experiment was conducted in which the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 351.77pt, "diffusion of a pigment was monitored between a donor compartment and an acceptor in the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 367.61pt, "form of a thin porous membrane. During the process, the pigment underwent chemical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 383.45pt, "degradation, forming a secondary species that was detected simultaneously using an additional ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.29pt, "probe beam. As a result, two independent release profiles were obtained, enabling the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 415.25pt, "determination of diffusion coefficients and decay rates separately in the donor and acceptor ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 431.09pt, "domains. Simplified versions of the model were also introduced to allow straightforward ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 446.93pt, "estimation of the key transport parameters. Finally, characteristic times associated with ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 462.79pt, "interfacial equilibration were determined based on photoacoustically detected changes in the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 478.51pt, "reflectivity of the donor–acceptor and acceptor–air interfaces. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
