  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 278.57pt, "The photoacoustic multi-beam modality involves multiple scanning beams applied ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 294.53pt, "simultaneously for the sample monitoring. In the case of divergent and relatively weak light ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 310.37pt, "sources (like LEDs for instance), i.e. where all the nonlinear effects are negligible, the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 326.21pt, "cumulative sample PA response is given simply by a sum of individual contributions to each ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 342.05pt, "excitation. If the excitations are characterized by various modulation frequencies, then the lock-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 358.01pt, "in process allows for an unambiguous differentiation of the contributions as long as the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 373.73pt, "frequency shift between the modulations exceeds the filter bandwidth.  ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 397.73pt, "A basic two-beam setup for the ")
