  #line-at(124.82pt, 335.93pt, "MBPA-based sorption profiles and the diffusion coefficient ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 359.81pt, "4.2.1 Basic approach to the mass release kinetics studied with MBPA ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 383.57pt, "A single beam PA modality with the front side detection has been employed into release kinetics ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.41pt, "studies for several times, with different irradiation sources ranging from UV to IR [17,24,25]. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 415.37pt, "In a typical experiment, an acceptor (membrane) is placed on a pigment donor substrate; a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 431.21pt, "concentration difference between the subsystems triggers molecular diffusion often considered ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 447.05pt, "as of Fickian character. By benefiting from the depth profiling PA method, whereby the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 462.91pt, "screening depth is adjusted by setting the correct light modulation frequency, it is possible to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 478.87pt, "monitor the total pigment content within a profile of interest. Figure 3a shows a general diagram ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 494.59pt, "of the mass release system used in photoacoustic studies. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 518.59pt, "The MBPA mass release experiment, which examined pigment transfer from a donor substrate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 534.43pt, "into an acceptor membrane using 360- and 430-nm probe beams, was performed using the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 550.27pt, "configuration shown in Fig. 3a. Modulation sweeps were performed between 30 logarithmically ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 566.11pt, "spaced frequencies ranging from 20 to 900 Hz. The modulation frequencies matching the whole ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 582.07pt, "15 µm membrane profile were found to be ~50 Hz, i.e. a cut-off frequency where the initial ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 597.91pt, "scan exhibited pseudo-linear character in the log/log (signal vs frequency) representation. These ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 613.99pt, "values allow the thermal diffusivity of the material to be determined, ")
