  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81.72pt, "The paper also employs quantification of sorption data using an electrical circuit-based model ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 97.7pt, "of diffusion-reaction transport. This model was specifically designed for degradable trace ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 113.54pt, "molecules following a single degradation pathway to a stable photoproduct, with mass transport ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 129.38pt, "occurring from a donor to an acceptor compartment. System dynamics are captured by an ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 145.22pt, "evolution matrix that couples the two molecular populations through decay rates and mass ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 161.18pt, "transfer coefficients—driven by concentration gradients and linked to diffusion coefficients via ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 177.02pt, "electrical circuit (EC) resistivities. A simplified version of the model, tailored to the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 192.86pt, "experimental conditions and valid for short times, was introduced and validated against data ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 208.7pt, "acquired via the membrane-based photoacoustic (MBPA) method. Although the mathematical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 224.66pt, "expressions governing the concentration evolution of the primary pigment and its photoproduct ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 240.5pt, "in the membrane were deliberately simple, the diffusion coefficients extracted from data-fitting ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 256.34pt, "exhibited promising agreement with predictions from the general model, particularly in terms ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 272.18pt, "of order of magnitude. Thus, the study establishes a robust, extensible modeling framework for ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 288.05pt, "quantitative analysis of mass transfer processes in applied physics contexts. ")
